75:## Buffer inventory and lifetime
79:Readers: O=model/device mapper/rollout observation storage; T=transition storage/GAE; D=diagnostics/reward oracle/evaluation. Outputs stay valid until the next `reset`/`step`/`truncate_envs` call, whose entry fence (R1) waits for every queued device read first; this is the contract's lifetime. CPU users copy any data they retain before the next call. Inputs are borrowed until the native call returns.
